{"title":"2023 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Faster)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Faster)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(THINKING_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (THINKING CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Similar_Triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn (Using Similar Triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove(Using_Area-Similarity_Relaitionship)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove(Using Area-Similarity Relaitionship)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_Magic_Square_(Using_Similarity_and_Special_Value)(best_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by Magic Square (Using Similarity and Special Value)(best solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_harungurcan\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by harungurcan</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Isosceles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has equal side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. In the figure below, segments are drawn parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> so that the shaded portions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> have the same area. The heights of the two unshaded portions are 11 and 5 units, respectively. What is the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />? (Diagram not drawn to scale.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/61696b1f6c1847f1610683505bd7e902290c51da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] //Diagram by TheMathGuyd size(12cm); real h = 2.5; // height real g=4; //c2c space real s = 0.65; //Xcord of Hline real adj = 0.08; //adjust line diffs pair A,B,C; B=(0,h); C=(1,0); A=-conj(C); pair PONE=(s,h*(1-s)); //Endpoint of Hline ONE pair PTWO=(s+adj,h*(1-s-adj)); //Endpoint of Hline ONE path LONE=PONE--(-conj(PONE)); //Hline ONE path LTWO=PTWO--(-conj(PTWO)); path T=A--B--C--cycle; //Triangle   fill (shift(g,0)*(LTWO--B--cycle),mediumgrey); fill (LONE--A--C--cycle,mediumgrey);  draw(LONE); draw(T); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE);  draw(shift(g,0)*LTWO); draw(shift(g,0)*T); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,shift(g,0)*A,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,shift(g,0)*B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,shift(g,0)*C,SE);  draw(B--shift(g,0)*B,dashed); draw(C--shift(g,0)*A,dashed); draw((g/2,0)--(g/2,h),dashed); draw((0,h*(1-s))--B,dashed); draw((g,h*(1-s-adj))--(g,0),dashed); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, midpoint((g,h*(1-s-adj))--(g,0)),UnFill); label(&quot;$h$&quot;, midpoint((g/2,0)--(g/2,h)),UnFill); label(&quot;$11$&quot;, midpoint((0,h*(1-s))--B),UnFill); [/asy]\" width=\"568\" height=\"262\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/61158bf35c5fd37cfd3fda3eac1332464a16b512.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 14.6 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 14.8 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 15 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 15.2 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 15.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"457\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we notice that the smaller isosceles triangles are similar to the larger isosceles triangles. We can find that the area of the gray area in the first triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/a/b5a63d43804c4180fde2eae4c1b2e6762809ebda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]\\cdot\\left(1-\\left(\\tfrac{11}{h}\\right)^2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"161\" height=\"34\" />. Similarly, we can find that the area of the gray part in the second triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/3/4332abc36dbe7b46581835c8d767bae47dc2fb7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]\\cdot\\left(\\tfrac{h-5}{h}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"120\" height=\"27\" />. These areas are equal, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bf358528730ca3007b2447d662de59179a26c1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\left(\\frac{11}{h}\\right)^2=\\left(\\frac{h-5}{h}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"193\" height=\"48\" />. Simplifying yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcfd5623da783d25337f4b3fadc90d4a35c19a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10h=146$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce62f051c4e6c668b3ddb866869e01078c1c8f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }14.6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"116\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~MathFun1000 (~edits apex304) (~extra edits AVTV)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can call the length of AC as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the length of the base of the triangle with height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c1ad3f4e0680ff2f13852edfcdd850f2994fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{H} = \\frac{A}{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"39\" />. Therefore, the base of the smaller triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6eb9b7d4c066aff3c544a1daa33a0100bae17df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11X}{H}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"40\" height=\"39\" />. We find that the area of the trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/6291e13c85cee7fa38df7164a39a57a735491260.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{HX}{2}- \\frac{11^2X}{2H}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p>Using similar triangles once again, we find that the base of the shaded triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a5733550712833bd538a09a1bdf1e7ce446e04a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{H-5}{H} = \\frac{B}{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"39\" />. Therefore, the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be9ef721ff4a44ee6a7e6108d438fc5f7ee31930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(H-5)(HX-5X)/2H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"194\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Since the areas are the same, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a68a95a94999a1a7e79315fc9bf09fe0ab0183af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(HX)/2 - 121X/2H = (H-5)(HX-5X)/2H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"383\" height=\"20\" />. Multiplying each side by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af404afdcd6227f71e6ebc384ecf5826a8bf1c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/4039c1decfdb41a25f50059cebdbc2bcc24e33ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H^2x/X - 121X = h^2X - 5HX - 5HX + 25X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"372\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore, we can subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1a65623d474456a9b69025365ced1c9da3b8f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25X + H^2x/X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"21\" /> from both sides, and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a6a3e0a191d3c49e3acacfbd4d74a78385c7897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-146X = -10hx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" />. Finally, we divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/52969fdeeb90f7e24cd2a2f1a6cfe124776fee2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a9682351e0462ac0999c35e4bb31d2702809b91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10h = 146$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d3cfb5eeb174e8eb594b6bd9299349a8a0b6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}14.6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by CHECKMATE2021 (edits by someone that is unknown)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Faster)\">Solution 3 (Faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the length of AC does not matter, we can assume the height of triangle ABC is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. We assume that the bases of the first triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and the bases of the second triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41b37bf9aaa77552e07c8dc69fa8842f4d5fe13a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the area of the trapezoid in the first diagram is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e3b47e623ca5972a8973193b132cb8ac217d052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h^2}{2} - \\frac{11^2}{2} = \\frac{h^2-11^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"170\" height=\"41\" />. (Here we mean that the bases of the triangles are equivalent to its’ height.)\n</p><p>The area of the triangle in the second diagram is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9eeb2dd61ac27235f70daee4fb4d57bdc191a3d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(h-5)^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/8/1b8d687003ffdc1ed21cf67a3e2f9403c9317ee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h^2 - 11^2}{2} = \\frac{(h-5)^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"163\" height=\"41\" />. Multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/327edd11fe0cb8fe1bc20c4e31b58db8d76416f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2 - 121 = h^2 - 10h + 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"203\" height=\"18\" />. Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/214dfb490c7ab9be61d23e0e0985a1c5900633c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2 + 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> from both sides, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbdd5d0573898203ef827dac0369cb885a0e81d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-146 = -10h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d3cfb5eeb174e8eb594b6bd9299349a8a0b6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}14.6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:ILoveMath31415926535\" title=\"User:ILoveMath31415926535\">ILoveMath31415926535</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:CHECKMATE2021\" title=\"User:CHECKMATE2021\">CHECKMATE2021</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:London_System&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:London System (page does not exist)\">London_System</a>\n</p><p>Very minor edit by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Quetzalcoatlus&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Quetzalcoatlus (page does not exist)\">Quetzalcoatlus</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X\">Video Solution by Math-X</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ku_c1YHnLt0?si=NHwA1x9STOJLG8IP&amp;t=5349\">https://youtu.be/Ku_c1YHnLt0?si=NHwA1x9STOJLG8IP&amp;t=5349</a> \n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zntZrtsnyxc?si=nM5eWOwNU6HRdleZ&amp;t=2990\">https://youtu.be/zntZrtsnyxc?si=nM5eWOwNU6HRdleZ&amp;t=2990</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/uxyJGZ3ZYGE\">https://youtu.be/uxyJGZ3ZYGE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28THINKING_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(THINKING_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (THINKING CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (THINKING CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SVVSMcw1Xe8\">https://youtu.be/SVVSMcw1Xe8</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn_.28Using_Similar_Triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Similar_Triangles)\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn (Using Similar Triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\">